<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Metzger et al. (2008) & Menshykau et al. (2012, 2014) mouse lung stereotyped branching modes (Domain D, Planar P, Orthogonal O), FGF10-SHH-Ptch1 Turing mode selection, pleura-confined diffuse-domain FGF10 cavity and stochastic postnatal septation — Code-to-model traceability: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring (L1-66) maps every section to its source and to the five Lean laws, and names the honest reduction of each Pass 3 item; section banners for 3b and 4b (L612-636, L1046-1065) carry the model equations; every new function has a docstring citing the equation or phase it implements; the math KG loop file (115 lines) registers Laws 4-5 with Lean theorem names, Lean code excerpts and Python code loci, and the loci of Laws 1-3 were refreshed to the new line numbers. Deductions: the self_test docstring (L1897-1906) still describes the Pass 2 7-item list and omits blocks 7-8 (-2); the tuned-constant comment on L117 points to an external handoff note rather than stating the sensitivity in the code (-2); the `--self-test` help string still says 'Pass 2' (L2009) (-1); the measurement for the transition position attributes the 0.5 bound to Metzger Fig. 3 in its `reference_source` string before admitting it is assigned (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py L1896–L1906: self_test docstring still lists the Pass 2 seven items; blocks 7-8 undocumented in the docstring <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py#L1896-L1906>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-code-traceability-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-code-traceability-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Metzger et al. (2008) & Menshykau et al. (2012, 2014) mouse lung stereotyped branching modes (Domain D, Planar P, Orthogonal O), FGF10-SHH-Ptch1 Turing mode selection, pleura-confined diffuse-domain FGF10 cavity and stochastic postnatal septation — Model fidelity to source: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The Metzger (2008) 3D D/P/O grammar with the 4m + 1 tip law and the Menshykau (2012, 2014) FGF10-SHH-Ptch1 dispersion relation are implemented as in Pass 2 (L183-442, L448-611). Pass 3 adds a genuine mechanism for the margin/interior mode switch: the ligand equation is solved in a diffuse-domain cavity (Li et al. 2009 formulation, Dirichlet F = 0 beyond the pleura via the (1 - psi) F / tau penalty, L656-702), the tip acts as a Ptch1 sink (R^2 = 1 + 3 exp(-r^2/0.25^2)), and the P/O decision is the sign of the supply anisotropy (`decide`, L806-839); the solver is checked against the exact slab closed form with monotone first-order convergence (L704-747). The septation module is an exact-increment Yule process with the Mund (2008) phase structure (L1106-1172) and its mean law is proved in Lean (Law 5). Deductions: the cavity is a quasi-2D cross-section with a prescribed 15 %/generation dilation (L780-782) rather than a 3D moving boundary, tips are not advected by grad F and the pleura does not respond to the tree (-2); the switch depends on the tuned pair h_mid = 1.0 / A_c = 0.05 (L117, L123) and on three further unsourced constants (L119-121) (-2); `simulate_fgf10_shh_mode_switch` clips R and F to [0.1, 3.2] every step (L578-579), uses an unjustified `diff_scale = 0.25` for the domain case (L568), and its seed profiles hard-code the final peak spacing, so the apical-vs-lateral outcome is largely prescribed by the initial condition (-2, pre-existing, not scored in Pass 2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py L116–L123: PLEURA_* and RECEPTOR_* constants: h_mid = 1.0 and A_c = 0.05 are tuned (comment on L117); growth 0.15, gamma 4.0, tip gain 2.0 unsourced <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py#L116-L123>",
        "2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py L568–L579: diff_scale = 0.25 for the domain case and per-step clipping of R, F to [0.1, 3.2] in the spectral Turing solver <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py#L568-L579>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-model-fidelity-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-model-fidelity-6> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Metzger et al. (2008) & Menshykau et al. (2012, 2014) mouse lung stereotyped branching modes (Domain D, Planar P, Orthogonal O), FGF10-SHH-Ptch1 Turing mode selection, pleura-confined diffuse-domain FGF10 cavity and stochastic postnatal septation — Morphometric validation: 87/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` reports 13 entries (L1739-1893): the 8 Pass 2 metrics plus the slab-check relative error 0.0261 (ref 0), the P/O transition position 0.54 (ref 0.5 convention), the emergent dihedral RMSE 3.13 deg (ref 0; 8/8 mode accuracy; non-circular, the observed dihedral is never fed back), the ensemble P36 alveolar count 2.32e6 (ref 2.3e6, explicitly labelled a calibration target) and the per-unit CV 0.9978 (ref 0.9999, Yule law). The lineage validation now grows each tree with the pleura policy instead of the observed dihedral (L969-1044), which closes the Pass 2 circularity. Deductions: the E11-E14.5 tip-count r = 1.0000 is self-referential because the benchmark event counts reproduce 2 + sum(D + P + O) exactly (`pred_tips`, L1004-1011) (-4); the `reference_value`s 0.481834 (isotropy contrast, L1838) and 1.4172 (lambda_T, L1848) are the model's own outputs recorded as references, unchanged since Pass 2 (-3); the adult alveolar count is fitted with 1 dof, so only the CVs, control, plateau and bulk/continued partition are tests and no per-age Mund (2008) count is compared (-3); the lung-level CV (0.028 vs 0.040 law) rests on 12 seeds and the self-test only bounds it below 0.1 (-1); the transition position reference 0.5 is a convention written into the dataset JSON, not a measured value (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py L1004–L1011: pred_tips = 2 + cumulative D+P+O events from the benchmark table whose event counts were back-filled to match, giving r = 1.0000 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py#L1004-L1011>",
        "2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py L1834–L1852: reference_value 0.481834 (L1838) and 1.4172 (L1848) are the script's own outputs, not literature values <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py#L1834-L1852>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-compound-lobar-scaffold-d-4-o-o-active-distal-tip-count-4m-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-diffuse-domain-fgf10-solver-relative-error-vs-closed-form-slab-profile-eps-0-025>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-emergent-pleura-confined-dihedral-rmse-vs-8-e12-5-e14-5-lineages>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-empirical-e11-0-e14-5-developmental-distal-tip-count-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-empirical-e12-5-e14-5-mouse-lung-dihedral-angle-rmse-8-lineages>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-fgf10-shh-ptch1-turing-critical-wavelength-lambda-t>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-optimal-dihedral-rotation-angle-delta-phi-maximizing-3d-inter-tip-clearance>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-planar-vs-orthogonal-transverse-3d-tip-isotropy-contrast-sigma-y-sigma-x>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-pleura-confined-margin-to-interior-p-o-transition-position-x-l-x>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-segmented-bronchial-daughter-to-parent-lumen-caliber-ratio-r-d-r-0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-segmented-mammalian-bronchial-tree-specimen-junction-angle-mean>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-septation-per-terminal-unit-alveolar-count-coefficient-of-variation-at-p36>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-stochastic-septation-adult-alveolar-count-at-p36-ensemble-mean>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-morphometric-validation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-morphometric-validation-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.7e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Metzger et al. (2008) & Menshykau et al. (2012, 2014) mouse lung stereotyped branching modes (Domain D, Planar P, Orthogonal O), FGF10-SHH-Ptch1 Turing mode selection, pleura-confined diffuse-domain FGF10 cavity and stochastic postnatal septation — MorphoEval overall 88.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3 remediated) evaluation of `2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py` (overall down slightly from 91.1 in Pass 2 despite both v2 remediation items being closed, because the round exposed defects that Pass 2 had not scored). The script now couples the Metzger (2008) D/P/O grammar to a diffuse-domain FGF10 cavity bounded by a dilating pleura (L612-963) so that the margin -> Planar / interior -> Orthogonal switch is emergent (position sweep x*/L_x = 0.54, critical half-thickness h* = 0.944 l0, slab-check error 0.026 with first-order convergence), replaces the circular Pass 2 lineage dihedral comparison with an emergent one (RMSE 3.13 deg, 8/8 mode accuracy, emergent isotropy vs hull flatness r = 0.996), and extends the grammar beyond E16.5 with an exact-increment Yule septation ensemble (632 units x 12 seeds, P36 = 2.32e6 vs the 2.3e6 calibration target, unit CV 0.998 vs Yule 0.9999, deterministic no-septation control frozen at 632). Five Lean 4 theorems (0 `sorry`s) are machine-checked, 13 morphometrics are measured, and the 8-block self-test passes in ~4.4 s with two-run bitwise determinism. Against that: the pleura half-thickness and anisotropy threshold are tuned so the transition sits mid-lobe; each lineage's lobe position is assigned from its class label; the E11-E14.5 benchmark table has no per-row provenance and its r = 1.0000 tip-count fit is self-referential; two Pass 2 reference values are the model's own outputs; the Turing PDE clips R and F to [0.1, 3.2] every step and its seed profiles prescribe the final peak spacing; `--seed` is parsed but never used; and the three new DOIs are unverified. Overall 88.5/100 (faithfulness 87.1, reproducibility 91.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 028758bc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 92, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 87, Source and data traceability 89, Code-to-model traceability 93, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes_comparison.png: rendered output of 2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py at 028758bc, image/png, 760057 B, 2950×1350 px, artifact_sha256 39a638e50c464718f55cb5a04c00c6dbe57169032a3a3896d1e76a6400bec3d4 (sha256 39a638e50c464718f55cb5a04c00c6dbe57169032a3a3896d1e76a6400bec3d4), spec_fingerprint d02b0c3844bcaa108ea9ec4bb8fce374a8da22fe6801db1a8256bba00a9e901f. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: d02b0c3844bcaa108ea9ec4bb8fce374a8da22fe6801db1a8256bba00a9e901f; artifact_sha256: 39a638e50c464718f55cb5a04c00c6dbe57169032a3a3896d1e76a6400bec3d4; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes/bronchial_tree_specimen.jpg=3247bc8c35eddcad..., datasets/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes_reference.json=860ab1e53046d2e7...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-lung-stereotyped-branching-modes-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Metzger et al. (2008): the E11-E15 mouse bronchial tree is built from three stereotyped subroutines — Domain Branching, Planar Bifurcation (confined to lobe edges/margins) and Orthogonal Bifurcation (lobe interiors) — composed in a genetically encoded sequence | Menshykau et al. (2012, 2014): an FGF10 / SHH-Ptch1 receptor-ligand Turing system on a growing epithelial domain selects between apical (bifurcation) and lateral (domain) budding, and mesenchymal geometry biases the direction of outgrowth | Mund, Stampanoni & Schittny (2008): mouse alveolarisation proceeds in a bulk phase P4-P21 and a continued phase P14-P36; Knust et al. (2009): the adult C57BL/6 mouse lung holds ~2.3e6 alveoli; reconstructed_in_script: 3D Bishop-frame D/P/O grammar with the 4m + 1 tip law and a 181-point dihedral sweep; the Menshykau dispersion relation and a 1D spectral PDE mode switch; a quasi-2D diffuse-domain FGF10 cavity bounded by a dilating lens-shaped pleura with the tip as Ptch1 sink, whose supply anisotropy chooses P (0 deg) vs O (90 deg) at each bifurcation; an exact-increment Yule septation ensemble seeded by the grammar's extrapolated E16.5 terminal-unit count; chromatic segmentation and skeletonisation of a bronchial-tree image; transfer_boundary: The pleura model is a transverse cross-section (z-invariant) with a prescribed, tree-independent dilation; tips choose P/O from the field but are not advected by grad F, and the pleura does not deform in response to the tree — the v2 item asked for a 3D moving-boundary phase-field/BEM, which this is not | lambda_bulk is fitted to the adult alveolar count, so the P36 total is a calibration, not a prediction; the 632 terminal units at E16.5 are a log-linear extrapolation of the vendored E11-E14.5 timecourse table; lambda_cont / lambda_bulk = 0.12 and birth at E19.5 are assumptions | The 'specimen' is a Wikimedia medical illustration of human bronchioles/alveoli, not a mouse E11-E15 lung; its junction angles are compared with the model's reference angles but cannot validate the mouse grammar; does_not_claim: A 3D moving-boundary mesenchyme, tip chemotaxis, per-age alveolar counts from Mund (2008), digitised Metzger (2008) lineage coordinates, or an independent prediction of the adult alveolar number." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py:1-26, 1806 and lung_stereotyped_branching_modes_reference.json:29-42 — the Li (2009), Mund (2008) and Knust (2009) DOIs are cited from memory and flagged unverified; Yule (1925) has no DOI. Verify the three DOIs against the publishers' records when network access is available, add the Yule (1925) DOI (Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 213:21-87), and clear the `verification` flags.",
        "remediation needed: 2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py:1004-1011 and 1834-1852 — the E11-E14.5 tip-count r = 1.0000 is self-referential (benchmark event counts reproduce 2 + sum(D+P+O) exactly) and reference_value 0.481834 / 1.4172 are the model's own outputs recorded as references. Digitise the observed tip counts from Metzger (2008) Fig. 1 with per-stage provenance and replace the two self-referential reference_values with literature values or mark them `reference_source: model` so the measurement is not read as a validation.",
        "remediation needed: 2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py:1116-1191 — lambda_bulk is fitted (1 dof) to the Knust (2009) adult count, so the P36 total is a calibration; lambda_cont / lambda_bulk = 0.12 and birth at E19.5 are assumed; no per-age alveolar count is compared. Transcribe the Mund (2008) per-age alveolar numbers (P4, P7, P10, P14, P21, P36) into the dataset JSON with figure provenance, fit lambda_bulk on the early points only and hold out the later ones as a prediction.",
        "remediation needed: 2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py:116-123 and 780-782 — h_mid = 1.0 and A_c = 0.05 are tuned so the single-tip P/O transition lands at x*/L_x = 0.54 (h_mid = 0.9 makes the whole lobe planar, 1.1 flips only the outer 10 %); the cavity dilation 0.15/generation, gamma = 4.0 and tip gain 2.0 are unsourced. Add a 2D sweep of (h_mid, A_c) reporting x* and the lineage mode accuracy as a function of both, source h_mid from a measured E12.5 lobe section aspect ratio, and state the sensitivity in the code rather than in an external note.",
        "remediation needed: 2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py:2024 and 2033-2047 — `--seed` is parsed but never passed to render_outputs, so RANDOM-RANDOM control trees always use seed 2008. Forward the seed (also to run_dihedral_angle_sweep and simulate_postnatal_septation) and add a self-test asserting that two different seeds change the random control but not the deterministic metrics.",
        "remediation needed: 2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py:553-579 — the spectral Turing solver clips R and F to [0.1, 3.2] every step, the seed profiles hard-code the final peak spacing (1.42 / 0.80), and diff_scale = 0.25 is applied only to the domain case; Panel C (ax_c, L1483) shows the traces saturating at the clip bounds. Remove the clipping (or justify it as a positivity projection and report how often it binds), seed from small random noise with a fixed RNG, and derive the domain/apical diffusion contrast from the Menshykau (2014) geometry rather than a constant.",
        "remediation needed: 2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py:841-844 and 969-1044 — the per-lineage emergent dihedral uses a single isolated tip at generation 1 while the flatness comparison uses the full policy tree; the two can disagree at mid-lobe positions (tree mean 45 deg). Report both predictors per lineage, flag disagreements, and add Panel G legend/inset placement that does not occlude the lens or the upper-right cavity.",
        "remediation needed: 2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py:989 with lung_stereotyped_branching_modes_reference.json:123-221 — `lobe_cross_section_position_norm` (0.90 margin / 0.15 interior) is assigned from the Metzger lineage class, so the 8/8 emergent mode accuracy tests 'margin -> planar, interior -> orthogonal' given the label. Replace the assigned positions with coordinates digitised from Metzger (2008) Fig. 3 lineage maps (or an independent lobe atlas) with per-row figure provenance, and report accuracy on positions that were not used to build the model.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes/bronchial_tree_specimen.jpg with 2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py:1237-1346 and 1874-1891 — the SHA-256-pinned 'specimen' is a human medical illustration (Lynch/Jaffe), not a mouse E11-E15 lung, so the junction-angle and caliber comparisons are drawing-vs-model. Add a CC-licensed mouse embryonic lung image (e.g. an E12.5-E14.5 whole-mount or lobe section) as a second pinned specimen, segment it, and compare the emergent P/O trees and the lens cross-section aspect ratio against it; keep the current image but relabel it as an illustration." ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.85e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Metzger et al. (2008) & Menshykau et al. (2012, 2014) mouse lung stereotyped branching modes (Domain D, Planar P, Orthogonal O), FGF10-SHH-Ptch1 Turing mode selection, pleura-confined diffuse-domain FGF10 cavity and stochastic postnatal septation — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2's dihedral sweep, mode-sequence comparison and equal-diffusion control remain (L385-442, L521-611). Pass 3 adds two genuine mechanistic sweeps: the subtree root across the lobe cross-section x0/L_x in [0, 0.9] with emergent dihedral, tree isotropy and anisotropy reported (margin-interior transition x*/L_x = 0.54; L880-925), and the lobe half-thickness with a critical h* = 0.944 l0 and monotone anisotropy (L928-963); plus a far-tip FGF10 ablation and the deterministic no-septation control (L1175-1191). Four new CLI flags (`--pleura-half-thickness`, `--anisotropy-threshold`, `--septation-seeds`, `--septation-cont-fraction`, L2017-2023) are wired through `render_outputs` (L2033-2047). Deductions: `--seed` (L2024) is parsed but never passed to `render_outputs`, so the RANDOM trees always use the hard-coded 2008 seed (-4); the anisotropy threshold and tip gain are swept only implicitly through the position sweep, and no sweep shows how x* moves with A_c or h_mid even though the handoff documents that it is sensitive to them (-4); the septation continued/bulk ratio is a CLI input, not a swept or fitted quantity (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py L2033–L2047: render_outputs call: pleura and septation flags forwarded, args.seed not forwarded (dead flag) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py#L2033-L2047>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-repro-package> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Metzger et al. (2008) & Menshykau et al. (2012, 2014) mouse lung stereotyped branching modes (Domain D, Planar P, Orthogonal O), FGF10-SHH-Ptch1 Turing mode selection, pleura-confined diffuse-domain FGF10 cavity and stochastic postnatal septation — Reproducibility package: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`--self-test` passes in ~4.4 s with 8 blocks (L1896-2004): SHA-256 integrity, 4m + 1 law, dihedral optimum, Turing dispersion and equal-diffusion ablation, lineage correlation, specimen segmentation, two-run bitwise determinism, and the new block 7 (slab convergence < 5 %, centre -> orthogonal / margin -> planar, anisotropy monotone, 0.3 <= x* <= 0.9, 8/8 mode accuracy, far-tip ablation, determinism; L1953-1976) and block 8 (mean-field agreement < 6 %, frozen control, no alveoli before P4, unit CV in [0.8, 1.2], lung CV < 0.1, P36 within 6 % of target, exact closed-form calibration, determinism; L1978-2003). The default render regenerates both media files in ~5.3 s; the pinned environment (Python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0) matches the venv. Deductions: the dead `--seed` flag means a documented reproducibility control does nothing (-3); the lung-CV bound (< 0.1) and the P36 tolerance (6 %) are loose relative to the reported values (-2); `docs/media` is git-ignored so the regenerated PNG/GIF are not pinned by hash in the repository (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py L2024–L2024: --seed parsed with default 2008 but never forwarded to render_outputs <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py#L2024-L2024>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-repro-package-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-repro-package-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-source-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Metzger et al. (2008) & Menshykau et al. (2012, 2014) mouse lung stereotyped branching modes (Domain D, Planar P, Orthogonal O), FGF10-SHH-Ptch1 Turing mode selection, pleura-confined diffuse-domain FGF10 cavity and stochastic postnatal septation — Source and data traceability: 89/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The dataset directory keeps the SHA-256-pinned specimen and JSON (runtime check `verify_dataset_integrity`, L145-167), and the JSON (307 lines, dataset_id -v2) now carries three additional sources, a `lobe_cross_section_position_norm` per lineage row, a `pleura_confinement_reference` block that states plainly that the position is ASSIGNED from the Metzger lineage class and that the paper gives no quantitative pleural distance (L274-287), and a `postnatal_alveolarization_reference` block (L288-307); `paper_citations.bib` gains three entries (L47-81) and the README is updated. The header docstring lists all 7 sources with DOIs (L1-26). Deductions: the three new DOIs (Li 2009, Mund 2008, Knust 2009) were cited offline from memory and are flagged `unverified` in the JSON (L29-42), bib and docstring (L26) — they could not be checked in this audit either (-4); the `empirical_mouse_lung_lineage_benchmarks` and `developmental_timecourse_e11_to_e15` tables (L110-273) still have no per-row figure/table provenance and their hull-flatness values look synthetic (-4); Yule (1925) is cited in a measurement source without DOI (L1806) and `margin_position_norm_min = 0.5` (L277) is a convention presented alongside paper-derived values (-2); the specimen's Wikimedia provenance is correct but the image is not of the organism studied (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "datasets/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes_reference.json L110–L273: Lineage benchmark and E11-E15 timecourse tables without per-row figure/table provenance <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/datasets/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes_reference.json#L110-L273>",
        "datasets/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes_reference.json L27–L42: Three new sources each carrying `verification: cited offline from memory in Pass 3; DOI unverified` <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/datasets/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes_reference.json#L27-L42>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-source-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-source-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-source-traceability-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-source-traceability-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-specimen-match> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Metzger et al. (2008) & Menshykau et al. (2012, 2014) mouse lung stereotyped branching modes (Domain D, Planar P, Orthogonal O), FGF10-SHH-Ptch1 Turing mode selection, pleura-confined diffuse-domain FGF10 cavity and stochastic postnatal septation — Morphological realism / specimen match: 82/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The segmentation pipeline (chromatic tissue separation, EDT caliber map, Zhang-Suen skeleton, N = 32 three-arm junctions, mean angle 76.49 +/- 14.61 deg, caliber ratio 0.8826, L1197-1346) runs unchanged and the figure now carries 8 panels with Panel G (cavity field, pleura contour, candidate tips, position-sweep inset) and Panel H (log-scale tips/alveoli timecourse with ensemble band, control and target lines, phase shading) rendered from the new modules (L1567-1657). Deductions: `bronchial_tree_specimen.jpg` is a Wikimedia medical illustration of human bronchioles and alveoli, not a mouse E11-E15 lung, so the junction-angle comparison is a drawing-vs-model match and cannot validate the Metzger grammar (-8; this was present in Pass 2 but not scored); the Pass 3 morphologies (lens cross-section, septated terminal units) are compared with no image of a mouse lobe section or alveolar histology (-5); Panel G's legend overlaps the lens and its inset covers the upper-right cavity (-2); the emergent P/O choice per lineage uses a single isolated tip (L841-844) while the flatness comparison uses the full policy tree, and the two predictors can disagree for mid-lobe positions (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py L1874–L1891: Junction-angle and caliber measurements derive from Wikimedia File:Bronchial_anatomy.jpg, a human medical illustration, not a mouse specimen <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py#L1874-L1891>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-specimen-match-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

